---
// Legend-as-art (Lupi) — verbatim from 07 §5.5. Rest-of-U.S. row reads
// "everywhere outside the 31 metros" (the fix vs the prototype's "top 30").
---

<div class="card legendcard">
  <span class="hand">the key</span>
  <span class="anno">← cool comes, warm goes</span>
  <div class="row">
    <svg width="112" height="10" aria-hidden="true">
      <defs
        ><linearGradient id="lgin"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#EAE2D4"></stop><stop offset="1" stop-color="#2E93B4"
          ></stop></linearGradient></defs
      >
      <rect class="swatch" width="112" height="8" rx="4" fill="url(#lgin)"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span class="lg"><b>Arriving</b> — net gain of people</span>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <svg width="112" height="10" aria-hidden="true">
      <defs
        ><linearGradient id="lgout"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#EAE2D4"></stop><stop offset="1" stop-color="#D3823C"
          ></stop></linearGradient></defs
      >
      <rect class="swatch" width="112" height="8" rx="4" fill="url(#lgout)"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span class="lg"><b>Leaving</b> — net loss of people</span>
  </div>
  <div class="row">
    <span class="swatch" style="width:112px;background:var(--muted);opacity:.5"></span>
    <span class="lg"><b>Rest of U.S.</b> — everywhere outside the 31 metros</span>
  </div>
  <div class="foot">
    Colour carries direction; the sign (+/−) and labels repeat it, so it never rests on colour alone. Spectral <i
      >within</i
    > each pole shows magnitude.
  </div>
</div>
